    <!-- THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT. A comment placed ABOVE <Flow>
         breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with the misleading "unable to find matching
         parent xml file" error.

         =====================================================================
         2026-08-10 (Tranche 3C follow up) ENTRY CONDITION ADDED, fTitle WIDENED. NOTHING ELSE.
         =====================================================================
         Until this change the <start> element carried NO filters, NO filterLogic and NO
         filterFormula, so this flow fired on EVERY PSA_Version__c insert and notified BOTH
         Acquisitions_Team and Legal_Team. That was harmless only because no disposition PSA
         version had ever existed. THE C2 FIX IS EXACTLY WHAT MAKES THEM START EXISTING:
         PsaVersionService now accepts a sell side token and DispositionStageEntryService
         auto-creates a Disposition_PSA Contract Review on stage entry, so the first sell side
         redline would have told the acquisitions team about a sale.

         This is the IDENTICAL shape as flows/Counter_Offer_Notify, gated the same day as review
         critical C4. That review and design §4.12 named only the Counter Offer flow; this one is
         the same defect one object over, found by the 3C developer while fixing C2.

         🔴 THIS SUPPRESSES AN EXISTING NOTIFICATION. IT DOES NOT CREATE ONE. Read that before
         "restoring" the ungated start element. D9 puts every notification in this programme, all
         14 on the disposition side, OUT OF SCOPE, and D15 finding #4 states the distinction
         explicitly: "Gating that flow is scope CONTAINMENT, not a new notification, and is
         therefore not covered by D9's deferral." Removing this criterion does not restore parity;
         it re opens a cross module leak.

         =====================================================================
         THE TRAVERSAL NAME IS Contract_Review__r, AND IT IS NOT THE relationshipName.
         =====================================================================
         ⚠ Do not copy this name from the field file's <relationshipName>PSA_Versions</relationshipName>.
         That is the CHILD side name, used going parent to children
         (Contract_Review__c.PSA_Versions__r). The PARENT traversal used here is derived from the
         LOOKUP FIELD's own API name, PSA_Version__c.Contract_Review__c, giving Contract_Review__r.
         It is therefore NOT LOI__r, which is what the sibling Counter_Offer_Notify uses; the two
         flows are the same shape over different parents.

         The discriminator is on the PARENT, so a condition row cannot express it: a record
         triggered flow's CONDITION BUILDER offers only fields on the triggering object, and
         PSA_Version__c carries no Disposition lookup and no record types of its own (deliberately,
         per the Tranche 3 design, which keeps record types on Contract_Review__c and off its
         children). Reaching a related record is what FORMULA entry conditions exist for
         (Winter '23, "Use Formulas as Flow Entry Conditions"). Hence <filterFormula> rather than
         <filters>/<filterLogic>: the two are alternatives, never both.

         ⚠ ONE HOP ONLY, AND DELIBERATELY NOT A RECORD TYPE TEST.
         $Record.Contract_Review__r.Disposition__c is a single lookup traversal to a stored field.
         Contract_Review__r.RecordType.DeveloperName would be a SECOND hop and is not available in
         an entry formula, so keying on the lookup is not a preference here, it is the only
         expressible option. Contract_Review__c.Disposition__c's own field header states the same
         rule from the other end: "THE LOOKUP, NOT THE RECORD TYPE, IS THE DISCRIMINATOR anything
         outside the record page should test."

         ⚠ SECOND filterFormula IN THE REPO, after Counter_Offer_Notify. Neither is deployed yet.
         Confirm at check only that the element is accepted at API 67.0, and confirm in the org
         that an ACQUISITION PSA version STILL produces both notifications: an entry condition that
         silently matches nothing looks identical to a working gate from outside.

         =====================================================================
         IT FAILS IN THE SAFE DIRECTION, AND THE PARENT IS ALWAYS THERE.
         =====================================================================
         PSA_Version__c.Contract_Review__c is <required>true</required> with a Restrict delete
         constraint, so the traversal can never dangle. On an acquisition PSA the parent's
         Disposition__c is blank by construction (OpportunityReviewService creates acquisition
         Contract Reviews with only Opportunity__c set), so ISBLANK is TRUE, the flow fires, and
         Acquisitions_Team and Legal_Team are unaffected. The failure mode of a wrong answer is an
         extra notification to the existing audience, never a missing one.

         =====================================================================
         fTitle NOW TREATS 'Buyer' AS THE COUNTERPARTY. THAT IS A DIVERGENCE FROM C4, ON PURPOSE.
         =====================================================================
         The second order defect is the same one review C4 named on Counter_Offer_Notify: fTitle
         branched on Direction__c = 'Seller' only, and 3C added 'Buyer' as the sell side
         counterparty token, so a buyer's version fell to the else branch and announced "PSA
         version sent to seller" when the buyer sent it.

         On Counter_Offer_Notify that branch was LEFT ALONE because the gate was judged to remove
         the whole population that could reach it. HERE IT DOES NOT, so the same reasoning reaches
         the opposite answer. PsaVersionService.isSaleSide is RECORD TYPE FIRST and falls back to
         the lookup, so a Contract Review carrying the Disposition_PSA record type with a BLANK
         Disposition__c lookup is sale side to the SERVICE (it writes 'Buyer') and acquisition side
         to THIS GATE (ISBLANK is true, so the flow fires). The lookup is deliberately not required,
         so a hand created Disposition PSA reaches that state through the ordinary UI. The
         auto create path is safe (DispositionStageEntryService always sets Disposition__c), and a
         hand edited 'Buyer' on an acquisition version is the same narrow residual C4 recorded.

         The widening is a STRICT NO OP on every value the acquisition side actually produces:
         PsaVersionService stores 'Ours' or 'Seller' there, and both take exactly the branch they
         took before. Only 'Buyer', which was previously wrong wherever it appeared, changes. Both
         'Seller' and 'Buyer' mean THE COUNTERPARTY per the Direction__c token contract; 'Ours'
         means DPEG on either side.

         🔴 RESIDUAL, NAMED RATHER THAN FIXED: for that same blank lookup row the GATE also fails
         open, so Acquisitions_Team still hears about a sale, merely with a correct title now. This
         file cannot close that: the formula's only discriminator IS the blank lookup. The real fix
         is upstream, making Disposition__c required on the Disposition_PSA record type or having
         the service refuse a sale side write without it, and both are outside this one file edit.
         The else branch's "sent to seller" is likewise acquisition vocabulary and would name DPEG
         on a sale; it is left because the gate removes every sale the service can produce.
    -->
    <actionCalls>
        <name>Notify_Acquisitions</name>
        <label>Notify Acquisitions</label>
        <locationX>176</locationX>
        <locationY>288</locationY>
        <actionName>GroupNotifier</actionName>
        <actionType>apex</actionType>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Notify_Legal</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <flowTransactionModel>CurrentTransaction</flowTransactionModel>
        <inputParameters>
            <name>recipientGroup</name>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Acquisitions_Team</stringValue>
            </value>
        </inputParameters>
        <inputParameters>
            <name>title</name>
            <value>
                <elementReference>fTitle</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputParameters>
        <inputParameters>
            <name>body</name>
            <value>
                <elementReference>fBody</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputParameters>
        <inputParameters>
            <name>targetRecordId</name>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.Contract_Review__c</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputParameters>
        <nameSegment>GroupNotifier</nameSegment>
    </actionCalls>
    <actionCalls>
        <name>Notify_Legal</name>
        <label>Notify Legal</label>
        <locationX>176</locationX>
        <locationY>408</locationY>
        <actionName>GroupNotifier</actionName>
        <actionType>apex</actionType>
        <flowTransactionModel>CurrentTransaction</flowTransactionModel>
        <inputParameters>
            <name>recipientGroup</name>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Legal_Team</stringValue>
            </value>
        </inputParameters>
        <inputParameters>
            <name>title</name>
            <value>
                <stringValue>New PSA version logged</stringValue>
            </value>
        </inputParameters>
        <inputParameters>
            <name>body</name>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Compare this version against the executed LOI and prior redlines.</stringValue>
            </value>
        </inputParameters>
        <inputParameters>
            <name>targetRecordId</name>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.Contract_Review__c</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputParameters>
        <nameSegment>GroupNotifier</nameSegment>
    </actionCalls>
    <apiVersion>67.0</apiVersion>
    <description>Notifies Acquisitions_Team and Legal_Team when a PSA version is logged. Gated 2026-08-10 to ACQUISITION PSAs (Contract_Review__r.Disposition__c blank): that SUPPRESSES an over-broad existing notification, not a new one. Do not remove it.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <name>fBody</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>{!$Record.Name} &amp; IF(ISBLANK({!$Record.Summary__c}), &apos;&apos;, &apos;: &apos; &amp; LEFT({!$Record.Summary__c}, 200))</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>fTitle</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>IF(OR(ISPICKVAL({!$Record.Direction__c}, &apos;Seller&apos;), ISPICKVAL({!$Record.Direction__c}, &apos;Buyer&apos;)),
&apos;PSA version received - ball in our court&apos;,
&apos;PSA version sent to seller&apos;)</expression>
    </formulas>
    <interviewLabel>PSA Version Notify {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>PSA Version Notify</label>
    <processType>AutoLaunchedFlow</processType>
    <start>
        <locationX>50</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Notify_Acquisitions</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterFormula>ISBLANK({!$Record.Contract_Review__r.Disposition__c})</filterFormula>
        <object>PSA_Version__c</object>
        <recordTriggerType>Create</recordTriggerType>
        <triggerType>RecordAfterSave</triggerType>
    </start>
    <status>Active</status>
</Flow>
